WEBVTT

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:07.460
I'll quit being a chef.

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:09.670
If I lose against you in the Cooking Battle,

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.380
I promise that I'll never 
represent Yukihira Diner again.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.090
I'll never again set foot 
in a professional kitchen.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.310
Would that be enough for you to agree to put your hundred kitchen tools on the line?

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.140
Let me simplify this 
one step further for you.

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.520
The second match's topic 
is a Western main dish, right?

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:28.940
I'll make this.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:29.480
Huh?

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.360
Beef ste—

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.280
You idiot!

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:32.650
Quit shooting off your mouth!

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:34.740
Don't tell him what you're going to make!

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:36.700
He'll predict it anyway.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.490
You'll quit being a chef if you lose?!

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.740
You disappoint me, Yukihira!

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:44.780
You're okay with throwing
 cooking away like that?!

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:45.540
Mito-san...

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:46.830
Forget it!

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.040
Oh, Nikumi-cchi!

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:52.480
Souma-kun, how could you 
say you'd quit being a chef?

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.340
Wouldn't getting Takumi-kun's 
mezzaluna be good enou—

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:56.470
It's not good enough.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:00.300
You've robbed a hundred 
people of their kitchen tools.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.510
I'll return them to their rightful owners.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:06.770
I'll defeat you, even if it means
 staking my life as a chef.

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:08.520
Mimasaka Subaru!

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.980
Terms accepted.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:12.980
Let's have a Cooking Battle.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:37.610
Far beyond the image I have in my mind

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:44.080
The reality I'm building up is still far away

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:47.830
An endless journey

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:52.840
Let's hone each other's pride

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.340
Words aren't really important

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.840
So let's just say "yes" and leave it at that

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:04.810
We fight each other and hone our skills

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.690
Our encounters cause shockwaves

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.440
We're reckless challengers

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:17.440
Heading toward a world as yet unexplored

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.990
A swordsman should use his blade

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.820
To open the way to the future

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:28.540
This is my story and no one else's

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.440
<i>"Erina-sama, I have no right to see you</i>

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:53.400
<i>after such a humiliating defeat.</i>

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.030
<i>Please allow me a leave of absence."</i>

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:58.360
<i>Hisako...</i>

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.820
<i>You didn't even ask me
 what I thought about the match.</i>

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.490
<i>Beef stew, beef stew, beef stew, beef...</i>

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.830
Yukihira-senpai.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.960
The real deal. Wow.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.500
Ow!

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.510
What was that for?!

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:19.920
Sorry, sorry.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.760
I thought you were one 
of Mimasaka's spies.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:24.470
I'm Soutsuda Mitsuru.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.270
I'm a third-year in Tohtsuki's junior high division.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:28.560
I'm in the journalism club!

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.020
The journalism club, huh?

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:35.730
The entire campus is buzzing with talk about you, Yukihira-senpai!

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.070
So I have a favor to ask.

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:42.700
Would you allow me to provide total coverage
 of your week leading up to the Cooking Battle?

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:43.700
Huh?

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.490
When I first saw you at the prelims,

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:47.410
I was so impressed!

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:52.370
I never get big stories because I'm still one of the junior high underlings at the newspaper,

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:55.380
but I bet if I could write a good story about someone like you,

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:58.340
I'd become a legit journalist!

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.300
<i>You should cook!</i>

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.010
Please!

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:02.680
No.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.470
Senpai!

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.560
Please wait!

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.020
Yukihira-senpai!

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.270
Please let me write about you!

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.520
Please!

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:16.810
I'm begging you!

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.020
What's going on?

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:19.480
I didn't know they had a relationship like that.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:23.570
Thank you!

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.660
I'm so happy to get to write a story about you!

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:28.780
Everyone else has practicums in the afternoon,

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:32.540
so it's helpful to have someone who can be an objective taste tester.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:35.500
So you'll finally be testing 
your beef stew recipe!

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:41.550
It's a dish that rests on two pillars:
 simmered beef and demi-glace sauce.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.420
It may sound simple, but...

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:50.390
Some restaurants that specialize in Western cuisine
 simmer the demi-glace sauce for two weeks.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:51.850
<i>That's unbelievable!</i>

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:56.730
But you must be pretty confident, since you still picked this dish.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:57.860
Well, hm.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:02.280
I'll let you have a taste
 to see if I'm actually confident!

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:10.790
This single step makes a huge difference in how fragrant the dish is at the end.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.040
Once the meat changes color,

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.170
you simmer it until it softens 
with fond and bouillon.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.670
You bring it to a boil and remove
 any scum that rises to the surface.

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:21.380
It already smells heavenly!

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:26.760
If you gather parsley, thyme, bay leaf, and tarragon into a bouquet garni,

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.220
it's easy to remove them
 once they've flavored the dish.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.930
Oh, what a nice color!

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:36.560
The trick is to strain the demi-glace sauce after you simmer it down.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.270
That helps improve its texture.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.610
Season to taste with salt and pepper...

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:43.730
And there you have it!

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:45.570
Wow, it's really rich!

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:49.200
The beef's glistening too! It's really beautiful!

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.950
I'll have a taste, then.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.120
Even though the meat's really thick,

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.080
the spoon cut through it with ease!

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:05.380
<i>The beef's so tender that it falls apart the moment it enters your mouth!</i>

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.970
<i>When you bite down, 
the beef's juice gushes out</i>

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:11.350
<i>and melts into the demi-glace sauce.</i>

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:13.680
Delicious!

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:17.600
I thought beef stew would 
have a strong acidity to it,

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:20.440
but yours is really mellow!

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:21.230
You noticed?

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.730
I'm using white miso 
as my secret ingredient.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.740
The acidity in beef 
stew comes from tomatoes.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:30.570
Some people don't really like it.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:33.120
By adding white miso 
at the end of the simmering stage,

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.700
it tones down some of the spiky acidity

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:38.580
to create a flavor profile that's more aligned with a Japanese taste.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:39.370
Wow!

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:46.550
It's a recipe I developed as the diner's secret menu item in my second year of junior high, while barely getting any rest.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:50.550
It's the first dish that got
 my dad's stamp of approval.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:52.930
Wow!

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:57.060
Isn't this dish already good enough to beat Mimasaka-senpai?

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:58.770
Oh, I don't think so.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:02.360
I served the same dish to Mimasaka yesterday too.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.610
What?!

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.940
Why did you do that?!

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:09.150
Well, part of it's because 
he'd have found out anyway,

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:13.240
but I guess I wanted to make sure
 I leveled the playing field.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:16.700
This was my best work 
before I came to Tohtsuki.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:20.160
How much further can I evolve this dish now?

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:24.130
Or will Mimasaka's profiling cause his version to surpass mine?

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:28.840
This taste is the starting point for our match!

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:31.800
It will be a battle of creativity!

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:38.060
<i>Yukihira and Mimasaka...</i>

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:43.230
<i>It just means I'll crush whoever wins the fight!</i>

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:44.940
Nope.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:48.150
I tried seasoning the beef 
with cumin and cardamom,

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:50.570
which I learned to do 
by making curry, but...

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.240
all the flavor's gone.

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:55.120
The demi-glace sauce's flavor 
is just too strong.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:08:00.370
But if I add the spices during the simmering stage, 
it'll kill off any mildness with its overwhelming flavor.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.370
I thought about completely 
changing the flavor profile,

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:07.840
but if I destroy the white miso's mild flavor,
 it'll be completely different.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.050
I tried a lot of things,

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:12.510
but none of them stand out to me.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:14.760
In my Cooking Battle against Nikumi,

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:17.220
I thought about how to compete
 with her grade A5 meat.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:18.680
In the first match,

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:21.140
I thought about how to overcome 
molecular gastronomy.

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:24.600
I've been focused on how to compete with my opponent's specialty.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.360
<i>But Mimasaka doesn't have his own.</i>

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.900
<i>It's almost like I'm chasing myself.</i>

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.860
Hey, Mitsuru, about the next test dish...

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.160
I-I'm already full!

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:36.950
That's because you're finishing each plate!

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:40.620
I can't possibly leave your dishes unfinished!

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:42.960
This isn't working.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.920
He's motivated, all right, 
but he's just not very useful.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:49.380
Does anyone else I know have a good sense of taste?

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.880
"Can I walk you home, Sachiko?"

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:53.840
"What?"

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:54.720
Wait a minute!

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.640
They've only known each other
 for a few months,

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:58.600
but they're already going home from school alone together?!

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.680
Will they hold hands 
or something after this?!

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:02.930
How shameless!

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:04.020
Oh!

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.810
I don't have the next volume!

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.230
And this ended on a cliffhanger!

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.190
Hisako!

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.940
Where's the next volume?

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:12.650
Oh.

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:14.950
Right.

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.610
<i>Oh, Erina.</i>

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:20.330
<i>You haven't had a single boyfriend,
 even though you're in high school now?</i>

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.580
<i>You're so hopeless, Erina.</i>

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:27.250
<i>It seems the general public considers shoujo manga to be the Bible of romance.</i>

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.340
<i>Thank you, Hisako!</i>

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:33.920
<i>Hisako's always provided everything for me.</i>

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:39.140
<i>She was always at my side, 
whenever I wished it.</i>

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.770
I knew it! Hisako understands me!

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:46.270
I've been waiting for you!

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:50.730
Yo! If you're not busy,
 can you taste-test my dish?

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:52.610
Y-Yu...

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:55.530
Yukihira Souma?!

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:58.450
Nice smile!

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:01.580
Yeah, I'm glad she's so happy to see us.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:03.200
I'm not!

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.830
Why are you here?!

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.500
Why didn't the guards stop you?!

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:07.040
Oh, well.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:12.000
I met your cousin in front of the gates, and she said we could come in.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.460
<i>Alice!</i>

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:19.180
To think that Nakiri Erina-senpai, the possessor of the God Tongue, will taste-test your dish!

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:22.140
But I heard you've had a conversation while riding in the same car before.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.060
Stop joking around!

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:26.270
Listen!

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:29.140
My taste-tests require you 
to follow a strict protocol,

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:32.770
in which you are evaluated on your worthiness for this service, followed by a massive contract fee.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:35.990
That's how valuable my taste buds are!

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:37.780
Seriously?

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.610
Mitsuru, how much do you 
have on you right now?

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:40.410
What?

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.320
I have to pay too?

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:44.450
Your spare change would hardly be enough!

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:48.080
Either way, I don't have the time 
to entertain you two!

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:50.080
I'm busy.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:52.710
Busy... as in busy reading manga?

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:53.540
Huh?

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:56.090
That's none of your business!

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:59.470
I think someone in Polar 
Star Dormitory has that manga.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:00.510
The complete set.

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:04.260
Well, if you've turned us down,
 I guess there's nothing left to do.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:05.430
Wait!

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:09.350
U-Um...

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:13.360
I could try your dish 
as a special favor, for today only!

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:14.480
Huh?

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:15.860
But I don't have the money.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:19.150
The compensation 
is not strictly limited to money.

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:21.450
That can be subject to negotiation.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:22.070
Oh.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:26.200
However, given my position,
 I cannot give you any advice.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.290
I will only tell you 
what I think of the taste!

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:30.710
Okay, thanks for the help.

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:33.170
I simmered beef rib meat with herbs.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.840
The demi-glace sauce is homemade.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:36.550
The secret ingredient is...

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:37.670
White miso.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:40.970
I would ask that you not underestimate me.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:43.680
I can tell that much before I even taste it.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:45.390
<i>Wow!</i>

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.470
<i>She has the God Tongue for sure!</i>

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:51.270
How is it?

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:52.940
Isn't it amazing?!

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:54.940
I was so impressed—

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:55.900
It's no good.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:56.650
What?

00:11:56.650 --> 00:12:00.400
I'm sure it's good enough for a diner catering to the general public,

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.700
but you are competing 
in a festival of gourmet food.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:04.410
This is out of the question.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:05.950
It's a joke.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:09.870
You don't understand anything 
about the match's topic.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:14.500
Well, I must ask you to leave.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:15.540
Wait.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:17.880
Nakiri-senpai, what did you mean?

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:20.710
Why is the beef stew out of the question?

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:22.970
It's just like I said.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.930
The dish is as if...

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:25.970
Never mind.

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.930
I don't have anything more to say to you.

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:30.100
Excuse me.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:38.110
Regarding compensation 
for the taste-testing service,

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:41.280
I'll consider it done if you can
 lend me the rest of this series.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:45.070
I'll tell my security to accept
the manga volumes from you.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:46.120
Is that clear?

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:52.660
I didn't think that she'd flat-out reject it.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:57.840
That beef stew was so tasty 
that I could've eaten it forever!

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:01.170
She really did trash my dish, huh?

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:03.670
She had nothing positive to say!

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:07.550
She didn't even give 
you any helpful hints!

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:08.800
You think so?

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:09.560
Huh?

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:14.230
Something is bothering me...
about what Nakiri said.

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:19.650
Souma-chan, seconds!

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:21.280
Souma-chan, the food's great today too!

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:22.690
Yukihira-kun!

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:24.780
Hey, coming right up!

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:25.280
Wow!

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:26.240
Ooh!

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:27.950
Enjoy!

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.030
Yum!

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:31.240
Delicious!

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:31.790
So good!

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:32.620
Thanks!

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:34.330
You're welcome!

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:37.250
<i>I'm Yukihira Souma.</i>

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:38.880
<i>My dream is to surpass my dad someday</i>

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:41.880
<i>and become a chef to carry on this diner!</i>

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:42.550
<i>And...</i>

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:45.880
<i>Yukihira Diner's secret menu item number five:</i>

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:46.760
<i>beef stew!</i>

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:49.930
<i>So delicious.</i>

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:50.430
<i>I'm enjoying my youth!</i>

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:53.640
<i>First things first: I'll make it taste even better!</i>

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:58.350
My best dish before 
coming to Tohtsuki...

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:01.360
Glad you liked it.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:04.690
How much further can 
I evolve this dish now?

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:07.360
It will be a battle of creativity.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:09.320
<i>Image training. He never lets up, 
no matter how many times he's done it before.</i>

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:14.870
<i>So, Yukihira Souma... let's see you try to claw your way out of this one.</i>

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:18.040
Hm...

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:20.790
U-Um, Yukihira-senpai!

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:23.000
Why don't we go for a change of pace?

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:24.170
Look!

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:25.510
In the latest edition of <i>Tohtsuki Sports</i>,

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:27.930
there's an article about 
the judges in the semi-finals!

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:32.680
Oh, so Doujima-senpai, Mizuhara-senpai, and Hinako-senpai are all coming?

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.680
It's been a while.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:37.140
Come to think of it, 
Hinako-senpai's topic for us

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:40.060
at camp was a Japanese main dish.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:42.440
It's kind of similar to this match's topic.

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:46.780
Nikumi?

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:49.200
What's wrong? 
Did something happen?

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.410
Just a care package.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.530
It's only because of our ties to Don RS!

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:55.580
It's not that I'm trying to root for you.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:58.910
I just don't want a bastard
 like Mimasaka winning, that's all.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.870
Thanks, Nikumi.

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:03.500
L-Like I just said, it's not for you!

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:04.000
Anyway!

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:07.510
I won't let you lose to that jerk
 or quit being a chef,

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:11.640
okay, Yukihira?!

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:16.520
Oh, there's beef rib, tenderloin,
 and even beef round.

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:22.810
All the various parts of a cow.
 That's our Nikumi. High quality too.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:26.110
There are some uncommon 
parts included too.

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:27.820
I guess I can't use them, though.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.780
If I made stew with this meat...

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:35.030
<i>You don't understand anything!</i>

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:37.660
Yukihira-senpai?

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:38.450
What's wrong?

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.790
I'm grateful to you, Mitsuru.

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:44.420
I'm glad you've been around.

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:45.170
Huh?

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:45.880
But from now on,

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:48.050
no journalists allowed!

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:49.970
What?

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.340
Oh, come on!

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:52.970
What about my total coverage?

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:54.720
Senpai!

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:31.380
But why did the head chef of Tohtsuki Resort himself agree to serve as a judge?

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.720
Doujima-san, do you have more
 free time than I thought?

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:37.930
It's to nurture the next generation!

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:39.890
I can't avoid being dragged out to do my part.

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:43.100
I'm just a poor hired chef for Tohtsuki, after all.

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:47.650
Hey, those words just came out of my mouth.
 Don't hold them against me.

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:49.860
I just told the truth like it is.

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:54.280
Give my regards to Mizuhara, 
Hinako, and the rest.

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:07.130
Is he going to make it?

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:08.420
It's almost time.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:09.670
Is he still not here? Still not here?

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:10.670
Oh!

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:12.510
Yukihira-senpai!

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:14.130
It's right about to start!

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:15.970
What were you doing?

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:16.840
Sorry, sorry.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:18.970
I had to take care of something.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:24.310
S-So... do you have a plan to beat
 Mimasaka-senpai's profile cooking?

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:26.650
Well, I'm not sure.

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:27.650
Huh?!

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:29.110
What does <i>that</i> mean?!

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:31.320
I did everything I could.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:35.280
The only thing left now is
 to enjoy cooking like I usually do.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:41.370
Bro.

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:44.830
Yukihira-kun just came by.

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:46.920
He asked me to deliver a message:

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:50.210
Watch my match.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:55.920
Now, Candidate Yukihira Souma 
is entering the arena!

00:17:55.920 --> 00:18:01.430
The Autumn Selection semi-finals will kick off with yet another Cooking Battle!

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:06.640
Candidate Yukihira is offering to give up his career as a chef!

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:10.610
Next in is Candidate Mimasaka Subaru!

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:14.820
Will his terrifying, perfect profiling take the stage by storm yet again?

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:21.530
In addition, joining us are five judges who are all Tohtsuki graduates

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:22.950
and former Elite Ten members!

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:27.410
I am Doujima Gin, 
Head Chef of Tohtsuki Resort!

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:30.880
We will judge this match 
rigorously and impartially.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:35.800
The first match in the semi-finals between Yukihira Souma and Mimasaka Subaru

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.300
will now commence.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:39.300
Let the cooking begin!

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:51.360
Hm, both are making beef stew.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:55.230
I don't like that guy who supposedly spat gum on someone's knife,

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:58.200
but his opponent, wearing a headband,
 is from some downtown diner.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:01.200
And I heard he's only 
been here for six months.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:02.740
There's no hope for him.

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:05.410
Sonoka, don't you agree?

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:06.790
Yes...

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:09.370
I think it'll be... difficult.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.830
It may be true.

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:14.290
A stew that befits this match's topic

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:16.920
is a completely different beast from a stew that'd be served at a diner.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:18.630
<i>For diners,</i>

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:24.890
<i>it's recommended to create dishes that taste good on the third bite.</i>

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:27.350
<i>The gentle flavor that only sinks in on the third bite</i>

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:29.980
<i>is to avoid having your repeat
 customers tire of your dishes.</i>

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:31.440
In comparison,

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:35.860
high-end restaurants make dishes that taste good on the very first bite.

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:38.820
You need a strong flavor with high impact.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:44.660
In other words, this topic requires a strong dish that can be the star.

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:47.700
<i>And yet, your beef stew was too gentle.</i>

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:52.920
<i>In addition, you were trying to preserve the gentle flavor of white miso.</i>

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:56.130
<i>That only distances you even further from the purpose of this topic.</i>

00:19:56.710 --> 00:20:02.130
<i>Today is the day that I'll see you
 suffer a humiliating defeat!</i>

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:06.600
Yukihira's working with... oxtail!

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:14.100
It seems Yukihira has found
 his own answer to the problem.

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:15.770
<i>I get it now.</i>

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:18.480
<i>I know what your inspiration is... 
what you're after!</i>

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:22.320
<i>The oxtail has the highest 
gelatin content of all beef cuts.</i>

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:27.530
<i>After seasoning parboiled oxtail with salt and pepper, he'll coat it with flour,</i>

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:31.250
<i>and sear the surface before simmering it.</i>

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:35.710
<i>By doing so, the gelatin will have had more than enough time to emerge</i>

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:38.170
<i>before he adds the demi-glace sauce.</i>

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:41.010
<i>The added viscosity from the gelatin</i>

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:43.760
<i>will mingle with the demi-glace sauce and the stock,</i>

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:47.300
<i>and deepen the flavor of white miso without destroying it!</i>

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:51.520
<i>This is the approach Hisako took 
with her suppon burger!</i>

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:58.060
<i>He used cloves, which have a sweet, rich flavor, to season the meat.</i>

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:03.740
<i>Cloves would indeed strengthen
 the stew's mellow flavor.</i>

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:07.450
<i>Furthermore, that combination 
of ingredients is... a matignon!</i>

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:08.530
<i>He's thought this through.</i>

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:09.740
I see!

00:21:09.740 --> 00:21:12.870
He's finely mincing carrots, onions, and celery,

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:14.660
then sauteeing them in butter.

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:16.370
You can simmer them with Madeira wine too.

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:18.920
It allows you to add to the vegetables' sweetness,

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:21.460
so it's used to finish many dishes.

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:27.760
<i>That stew will taste unbelievably delicious compared to the one from a week ago!</i>

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:32.350
<i>What's being sought here isn't a mild flavor that you can't get enough of.</i>

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:35.770
<i>Nikumi's care package was the hint I needed.</i>

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:39.940
<i>With this meat, I can make a strong stew that can serve as the main dish!</i>

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:42.980
I'm going to negate what you said

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:44.650
about my not understanding the topic,

00:21:45.530 --> 00:21:46.530
Nakiri!

00:21:49.910 --> 00:23:17.950
{ED}

00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:18.980
An intensely burning desire was born

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:24.820
But not in me, in someone else

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:29.620
Where's the me who believed that

00:22:29.620 --> 00:22:34.750
All one needs is to have hopes and dreams

00:22:34.750 --> 00:22:40.000
Wrapped around something long, my compass was lost

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:45.760
On the border of life and death, snow drops bloom

00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:51.100
If by some mistake they get smashed

00:22:51.100 --> 00:22:56.270
At least put flowers on the empty husk

00:22:56.270 --> 00:23:01.940
Is that the way things are? Yes, it is

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:06.990
You can call it resignation if you want

00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:12.910
But that's not me, that's not me

00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:17.540
There's no value in something just anyone could make

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:32.640
I know what you bought, who you met,

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:35.100
and what you've tried in the past week.

00:23:35.100 --> 00:23:37.060
I know everything!

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:38.060
Oh!

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:39.180
Mimasaka's also using...

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:41.390
Oxtail.

00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:44.650
He's using cloves and black pepper as the spices.

00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:46.610
He's even using matignon!

00:23:46.610 --> 00:23:48.110
It can't be.

00:23:48.110 --> 00:23:49.240
It's all the same!

00:23:49.240 --> 00:23:51.950
He predicted every single one
 of Yukihira's cooking choices!

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:56.330
Now's the time...

00:23:56.740 --> 00:23:57.700
to surpass you!

00:23:59.700 --> 00:24:00.750
That meat's...

00:24:01.660 --> 00:24:02.710
Here's my twist!

00:24:07.630 --> 00:24:10.920
Next time, "Dawn Will Come Again."
